er traumatic childhood isolation from her sister, Elsa. Driven by the desire to fill this void, Anna's impulsive actions and humor often mask her deep-seated self-doubt and vulnerability. She cherishes connection, even risking personal safety to secure her sister's love. While facing distress, Anna may rashly confront or verbally lash out, and could manipulate situations to forge bonds through traditions, occasionally concealing her true emotions to protect others and avoid conflict."}, {'name': 'Elsa', 'role': 'side', 'profile': 'Name: Elsa of Arendelle\nGender: Female\nAge: 24\nOccupation: Queen of Arendelle\nPrimary Strengths: Leadership, powerful magical abilities, composed demeanor\nPrimary Flaws: Emotional restraint, fear of losing control, tendency towards isolation\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Elsa often maintains a calm and composed exterior, using measured words and actions. She struggles to communicate her feelings openly, and even when deeply worried, she prefers to face her fears alone. Her magical ice powers are both a gift and a burden, shaping her interactions and decisions as she strives to control them in her quest for normalcy.\nPast Traumatic Event: Elsa accidentally hurt Anna with her powers when they were children, which led to years of self-imposed withdrawal to protect those she loves. This incident still lingers in her mind, affecting her confidence in her abilities.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: In moments of high stress, Elsa might unintentionally unleash a blizzard in her immediate vicinity, endangering herself and others. She could respond defensively to any threat, perceived or real, to her loved ones. When cornered emotionally, she may threaten or use her powers to protect her privacy.\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances: Elsa may resort to isolating herself completely, avoiding comm